-- coa19-ch1-requirements.l4: Part 25, Chapter 1 (Companies registered in England and Wales or in Northern Ireland), cross-headings
-- "Requirement to register company charges", "Special rules about debentures", "Charges in other jurisdictions" and "Orders charging land: Northern Ireland":
-- ss 860 to 868, lines 11842-11931 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law as the text states it.
--
-- The text prints Chapter A1 (ss 859A to 859Q) and this Chapter side by side. It does not say which governs a charge created by a company registered in
-- England and Wales or Northern Ireland; each Chapter is encoded on its own words (finding 1 and fork F-C1 in NOTES.md).
--
-- SEAMS taken as inputs: `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` (coa16), `s 1121 the officer is in default` (coa24), `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` (keel).
-- "the prescribed particulars" are not set out in the Act's own text: the person states whether they were delivered.

§ `Part 25 Company charges -- Chapter 1 Companies registered in England and Wales or in Northern Ireland -- ss 860 to 868`

§§ `s 861 definitions (s 861(5) "company" and "charge" govern this Chapter)`

-- "company" means a company registered in England and Wales or in Northern Ireland
-- src:11874 | “company” means a company registered in England and Wales or in Northern Ireland.
@ref s 861(5) "company" means a company registered in England and Wales or in Northern Ireland (src:11874-11874)
GIVEN `the place where the body is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 861(5) the body is a company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place where the body is registered`
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means a company registered in England and Wales or in Northern Ireland"

-- src:11873 | “charge” includes mortgage, and
@ref s 861(5) "charge" includes mortgage (src:11873-11873)
GIVEN `the arrangement is a mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 861(5) the arrangement is a charge` MEANS
    IF `the arrangement is a mortgage`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“charge” includes mortgage"

§§ `s 860 Charges created by a company`

DECLARE `s 860(7) what the charge is` HAS
    `a charge on land or any interest in land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a charge for any rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a charge created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a charge for the purposes of securing any issue of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a charge on uncalled share capital of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a charge on calls made but not paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a charge on book debts of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a floating charge on the company's property or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a charge on a ship or aircraft, or any share in a ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a charge on goodwill or on any intellectual property` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:11855 | (7) This section applies to the following charges—
-- src:11856 | (a) a charge on land or any interest in land, other than a charge for any rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land,
-- src:11857 | (b) a charge created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale,
-- src:11858 | (c) a charge for the purposes of securing any issue of debentures,
-- src:11859 | (d) a charge on uncalled share capital of the company,
-- src:11860 | (e) a charge on calls made but not paid,
-- src:11861 | (f) a charge on book debts of the company,
-- src:11862 | (g) a floating charge on the company's property or undertaking,
-- src:11863 | (h) a charge on a ship or aircraft, or any share in a ship,
-- src:11864 | (i) a charge on goodwill or on any intellectual property.
@ref s 860(7) This section applies to the following charges (src:11855-11864)
GIVEN charge IS A `s 860(7) what the charge is`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 860(7) the charge is one to which section 860 applies` MEANS
    IF       (charge's `a charge on land or any interest in land` AND (NOT charge's `a charge for any rent or other periodical sum issuing out of land`))
         OR  charge's `a charge created or evidenced by an instrument which, if executed by an individual, would require registration as a bill of sale`
         OR  charge's `a charge for the purposes of securing any issue of debentures`
         OR  charge's `a charge on uncalled share capital of the company`
         OR  charge's `a charge on calls made but not paid`
         OR  charge's `a charge on book debts of the company`
         OR  charge's `a floating charge on the company's property or undertaking`
         OR  charge's `a charge on a ship or aircraft, or any share in a ship`
         OR  charge's `a charge on goodwill or on any intellectual property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to the following charges—": a scope list with no "only" (fork F-C2 in NOTES.md)

-- src:11845 | (1) A company that creates a charge to which this section applies must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with the instrument (if any) by which the charge is created or evidenced, to the registrar for registration before the end of the period allowed for registration.
@ref s 860(1) A company that creates a charge to which this section applies must deliver the prescribed particulars of the charge, together with the instrument, to the registrar for registration before the end of the period allowed for registration (src:11845-11845)
GIVEN `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the company creates a charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 860(7) the charge is one to which section 860 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 860(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 861(5) the body is a company` `the place where the company is registered`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means a company registered in England and Wales or in Northern Ireland"
        IF (NOT `the company creates a charge`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that creates a charge to which this section applies must deliver"
        IF `s 860(7) the charge is one to which section 860 applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a charge to which this section applies": whether the charge is one the section applies to is not decided by the list in subsection (7)

-- src:11846 | (2) Registration of a charge to which this section applies may instead be effected on the application of a person interested in it.
@ref s 860(2) Registration of a charge to which this section applies may instead be effected on the application of a person interested in it (src:11846-11846)
GIVEN `the person is a person interested in the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 860(2) registration may be effected on the application of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person interested in the charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the application of a person interested in it"

-- src:11847 | (3) Where registration is effected on the application of some person other than the company, that person is entitled to recover from the company the amount of any fees properly paid by him to the registrar on registration.
@ref s 860(3) Where registration is effected on the application of some person other than the company, that person is entitled to recover from the company the amount of any fees properly paid (src:11847-11847)
GIVEN `registration is effected on the application of some person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 860(3) the person is entitled to recover from the company the fees properly paid` MEANS
    IF `registration is effected on the application of some person other than the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where registration is effected on the application of some person other than the company"

-- src:11847 | (3) Where registration is effected on the application of some person other than the company, that person is entitled to recover from the company the amount of any fees properly paid by him to the registrar on registration.
@ref s 860(3) the amount of any fees properly paid by him to the registrar on registration (src:11847-11847)
GIVEN `registration is effected on the application of some person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fees properly paid by the person to the registrar on registration, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 860(3) the amount the person is entitled to recover from the company` MEANS
    IF `registration is effected on the application of some person other than the company`
    THEN JUST `the fees properly paid by the person to the registrar on registration, in pounds`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where registration is effected on the application of some person other than the company"

-- src:11854 | (6) Subsection (4) does not apply if registration of the charge has been effected on the application of some other person.
@ref s 860(6) Subsection (4) does not apply if registration of the charge has been effected on the application of some other person (src:11854-11854)
GIVEN `registration of the charge has been effected on the application of some other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 860(6) subsection (4) applies` MEANS
    IF `registration of the charge has been effected on the application of some other person`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) does not apply if registration of the charge has been effected on the application of some other person"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (6) says only when subsection (4) does not apply

-- src:11848 | (4) If a company fails to comply with subsection (1), an offence is committed by—
-- src:11849 | (a) the company, and
-- src:11850 | (b) every officer of it who is in default.
@ref s 860(4) If a company fails to comply with subsection (1), an offence is committed by the company and every officer of it who is in default (src:11848-11850)
GIVEN `s 860(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 859H(1)(b) the particulars and instrument were delivered before the end of the period allowed for registration` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 860(6) subsection (4) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 860(4) the company fails to comply with subsection (1), so that an offence is committed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 860(6) subsection (4) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) does not apply if registration of the charge has been effected on the application of some other person"
        IF `s 860(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (1)": there is no duty under subsection (1)
        IF `s 860(1) the company must deliver the prescribed particulars and the instrument to the registrar` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
        IF `s 859H(1)(b) the particulars and instrument were delivered before the end of the period allowed for registration` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 859H(1)(b) the particulars and instrument were delivered before the end of the period allowed for registration` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (1)": the company complied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period has not yet run out

-- src:11849 | (a) the company, and
@ref s 860(4)(a) the company (src:11849-11849)
GIVEN `s 860(4) the company fails to comply with subsection (1), so that an offence is committed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 860(4)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS `s 860(4) the company fails to comply with subsection (1), so that an offence is committed`

-- src:11850 | (b) every officer of it who is in default.
@ref s 860(4)(b) every officer of it who is in default (src:11850-11850)
GIVEN `s 860(4) the company fails to comply with subsection (1), so that an offence is committed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 860(4)(b) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    `s 859A both answers hold` (`s 860(4) the company fails to comply with subsection (1), so that an offence is committed`) (`s 859A both answers hold` `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` `s 1121 the officer is in default`)

-- src:11851 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:11852 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:11853 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 860(5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on conviction on indictment to a fine, on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (src:11851-11853)
`s 860(5) the penalties for the offence` MEANS
    LIST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
         , (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

§§ `s 861 Charges which have to be registered: supplementary`

