GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 862(1) this section applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 861(5) the body is a company` `the place where the company is registered`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means a company registered in England and Wales or in Northern Ireland"
        IF (NOT `the company acquires property`) OR (NOT `the property is subject to a charge`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company acquires property which is subject to a charge"
