§§ `s 863 Charge in series of debentures`

-- src:11888 | (2) The following are the required particulars—
-- src:11889 | (a) the total amount secured by the whole series, and
-- src:11890 | (b) the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series and the date of the covering deed (if any) by which the series is created or defined, and
-- src:11891 | (c) a general description of the property charged, and
-- src:11892 | (d) the names of the trustees (if any) for the debenture holders.
@ref s 863(2) The following are the required particulars (src:11888-11892)
GIVEN `the particulars give the total amount secured by the whole series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a covering deed by which the series is created or defined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give the date of the covering deed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give a general description of the property charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are trustees for the debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars give the names of the trustees for the debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 863(2) the particulars given are the required particulars` MEANS
    IF       `the particulars give the total amount secured by the whole series`
         AND `the particulars give the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series`
         AND ((NOT `there is a covering deed by which the series is created or defined`) OR `the particulars give the date of the covering deed`)
         AND `the particulars give a general description of the property charged`
         AND ((NOT `there are trustees for the debenture holders`) OR `the particulars give the names of the trustees for the debenture holders`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following are the required particulars—"

-- src:11887 | (1) Where a series of debentures containing, or giving by reference to another instrument, any charge to the benefit of which debenture holders of that series are entitled pari passu is created by a company, it is for the purposes of section 860(1) sufficient if the required particulars, together with the deed containing the charge (or, if there is no such deed, one of the debentures of the series), are delivered to the registrar before the end of the period allowed for registration.
@ref s 863(1) it is for the purposes of section 860(1) sufficient if the required particulars, together with the deed containing the charge (or, if there is no such deed, one of the debentures of the series), are delivered to the registrar before the end of the period allowed for registration (src:11887-11887)
GIVEN `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a series of debentures containing, or giving by reference to another instrument, a charge to the benefit of which the debenture holders of that series are entitled pari passu is created by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 863(2) the particulars given are the required particulars` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 859H(1)(b) the deed or one of the debentures was delivered with the particulars before the end of the period allowed for registration` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 863(1) delivery of the particulars with the deed or one debenture is sufficient for section 860(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a series of debentures containing, or giving by reference to another instrument, a charge to the benefit of which the debenture holders of that series are entitled pari passu is created by a company`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a series of debentures containing, or giving by reference to another instrument, any charge to the benefit of which debenture holders of that series are entitled pari passu is created by a company"
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a series of debentures"
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the instruments are "debentures" is s 738
        IF (`s 863(2) the particulars given are the required particulars` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 859H(1)(b) the deed or one of the debentures was delivered with the particulars before the end of the period allowed for registration` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is for the purposes of section 860(1) sufficient if": "sufficient if" states a sufficient condition, not a necessary one

-- src:11893 | (3) Particulars of the date and amount of each issue of debentures of a series of the kind mentioned in subsection (1) must be sent to the registrar for entry in the register of charges.
@ref s 863(3) Particulars of the date and amount of each issue of debentures of a series of the kind mentioned in subsection (1) must be sent to the registrar for entry in the register of charges (src:11893-11893)
GIVEN `the debentures are of a series of the kind mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 863(3) particulars of the date and amount of each issue must be sent to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the debentures are of a series of the kind mentioned in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of a series of the kind mentioned in subsection (1)": the duty is laid on issues of a series of that kind; the text says nothing of other issues

-- src:11894 | (4) Failure to comply with subsection (3) does not affect the validity of the debentures issued.
@ref s 863(4) Failure to comply with subsection (3) does not affect the validity of the debentures issued (src:11894-11894)
GIVEN `there has been a failure to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 863(4) the failure to comply with subsection (3) affects the validity of the debentures issued` MEANS
    IF `there has been a failure to comply with subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with subsection (3) does not affect the validity of the debentures issued"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no failure for subsection (4) to speak of

-- src:11895 | (5) Subsections (2) to (6) of section 860 apply for the purposes of this section as they apply for the purposes of that section, but as if references to the registration of a charge were references to the registration of a series of debentures.
@ref s 863(5) Subsections (2) to (6) of section 860 apply for the purposes of this section as they apply for the purposes of that section (src:11895-11895)
GIVEN `the debentures are of a series of the kind mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 863(5) subsections (2) to (6) of section 860 apply to the registration of the series of debentures` MEANS
    IF `the debentures are of a series of the kind mentioned in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of this section": the subsections apply for the purposes of this section, which concerns a series of the kind mentioned in subsection (1)

§§ `s 864 Additional registration requirement for commission etc in relation to debentures`

-- src:11897 | (1) Where any commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made either directly or indirectly by a company to a person in consideration of his—
-- src:11898 | (a) subscribing or agreeing to subscribe, whether absolutely or conditionally, for debentures in a company, or
-- src:11899 | (b) procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions, whether absolute or conditional, for such debentures,
-- src:11900 | the particulars required to be sent for registration under section 860 shall include particulars as to the amount or rate per cent. of the commission, discount or allowance so paid or made.
@ref s 864(1) the particulars required to be sent for registration under section 860 shall include particulars as to the amount or rate per cent. of the commission, discount or allowance (src:11897-11900)
GIVEN `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made, directly or indirectly, by a company to a person in consideration of his subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for debentures in a company, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 864(1) the particulars must include the amount or rate per cent. of the commission, discount or allowance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made, directly or indirectly, by a company to a person in consideration of his subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for debentures in a company, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for them`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any commission, allowance or discount has been paid or made either directly or indirectly by a company to a person"
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for debentures in a company"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the instruments are "debentures" is s 738

-- src:11901 | (2) The deposit of debentures as security for a debt of the company is not, for the purposes of this section, treated as the issue of debentures at a discount.
@ref s 864(2) The deposit of debentures as security for a debt of the company is not, for the purposes of this section, treated as the issue of debentures at a discount (src:11901-11901)
GIVEN `the debentures are deposited as security for a debt of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 864(2) the deposit is treated as the issue of debentures at a discount` MEANS
    IF `the debentures are deposited as security for a debt of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not, for the purposes of this section, treated as the issue of debentures at a discount"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says only what the deposit of debentures as security is not

-- src:11902 | (3) Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of the debentures issued.
@ref s 864(3) Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of the debentures issued (src:11902-11902)
GIVEN `there has been a failure to comply with section 864` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 864(3) the failure to comply with section 864 affects the validity of the debentures issued` MEANS
    IF `there has been a failure to comply with section 864`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of the debentures issued"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no failure for subsection (3) to speak of

§§ `s 865 Endorsement of certificate on debentures`

-- src:11905 | (2) But this does not require a company to cause a certificate of registration of any charge so given to be endorsed on any debenture or certificate of debenture stock issued by the company before the charge was created.
@ref s 865(2) this does not require a company to cause a certificate of registration to be endorsed on any debenture issued before the charge was created (src:11905-11905)
GIVEN `the debenture or certificate of debenture stock was issued by the company before the charge was created` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 865(2) the company is required to cause a copy of the certificate to be endorsed on the debenture` MEANS
    IF `the debenture or certificate of debenture stock was issued by the company before the charge was created`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this does not require a company to cause a certificate of registration of any charge so given to be endorsed on any debenture or certificate of debenture stock issued by the company before the charge was created"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says only that a debenture issued before the charge was created is outside subsection (1)

-- src:11904 | (1) The company shall cause a copy of every certificate of registration given under section 869 to be endorsed on every debenture or certificate of debenture stock which is issued by the company, and the payment of which is secured by the charge so registered.
@ref s 865(1) The company shall cause a copy of every certificate of registration to be endorsed on every debenture or certificate of debenture stock which is issued by the company, and the payment of which is secured by the charge so registered (src:11904-11904)
GIVEN `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the debenture or certificate of debenture stock is issued by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its payment is secured by the charge so registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 865(2) the company is required to cause a copy of the certificate to be endorsed on the debenture` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 865(1) the company must cause a copy of the certificate of registration to be endorsed on the debenture` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 865(2) the company is required to cause a copy of the certificate to be endorsed on the debenture` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this does not require a company to cause a certificate of registration of any charge so given to be endorsed"
        IF (NOT `the debenture or certificate of debenture stock is issued by the company`) OR (NOT `its payment is secured by the charge so registered`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on every debenture or certificate of debenture stock which is issued by the company, and the payment of which is secured by the charge so registered": the duty is laid on those debentures and the text says nothing of any other
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on every debenture or certificate of debenture stock": the duty is laid on debentures and certificates of debenture stock and the text says nothing of any other instrument
        IF `s 738 the instrument is a debenture` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the instruments are "debentures" is s 738

-- src:11906 | (3) If a person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the delivery of a debenture or certificate of debenture stock which under this section is required to have endorsed on it a copy of a certificate of registration, without the copy being so endorsed upon it, he commits an offence.
@ref s 865(3) If a person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the delivery of a debenture or certificate of debenture stock which under this section is required to have endorsed on it a copy of a certificate of registration, without the copy being so endorsed upon it, he commits an offence (src:11906-11906)
GIVEN `the person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the delivery of a debenture or certificate of debenture stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 865(1) the company must cause a copy of the certificate of registration to be endorsed on the debenture` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the copy is so endorsed upon it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 865(3) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the delivery of a debenture or certificate of debenture stock`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the delivery of a debenture or certificate of debenture stock"
        IF `s 865(1) the company must cause a copy of the certificate of registration to be endorsed on the debenture` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which under this section is required to have endorsed on it a copy of a certificate of registration"
        IF `s 865(1) the company must cause a copy of the certificate of registration to be endorsed on the debenture` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
        IF `the copy is so endorsed upon it` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the copy being so endorsed upon it"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:11907 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 865(4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale (src:11907-11907)
`s 865(4) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), NOTHING, FALSE

§§ `s 866 Charges created in, or over property in, jurisdictions outside the United Kingdom`

-- src:11910 | (1) Where a charge is created outside the United Kingdom comprising property situated outside the United Kingdom, the delivery to the registrar of a verified copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced has the same effect for the purposes of this Chapter as the delivery of the instrument itself.
@ref s 866(1) Where a charge is created outside the United Kingdom comprising property situated outside the United Kingdom, the delivery to the registrar of a verified copy of the instrument has the same effect for the purposes of this Chapter as the delivery of the instrument itself (src:11910-11910)
GIVEN `the charge is created outside the United Kingdom comprising property situated outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a verified copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced is delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 866(1) the delivery of a verified copy has the same effect as the delivery of the instrument itself` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the charge is created outside the United Kingdom comprising property situated outside the United Kingdom`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a charge is created outside the United Kingdom comprising property situated outside the United Kingdom"
        IF `a verified copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced is delivered to the registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no verified copy has been delivered

-- src:11911 | (2) Where a charge is created in the United Kingdom but comprises property outside the United Kingdom, the instrument creating or purporting to create the charge may be sent for registration under section 860 even if further proceedings may be necessary to make the charge valid or effectual according to the law of the country in which the property is situated.
@ref s 866(2) Where a charge is created in the United Kingdom but comprises property outside the United Kingdom, the instrument may be sent for registration under section 860 even if further proceedings may be necessary (src:11911-11911)
GIVEN `the charge is created in the United Kingdom but comprises property outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 866(2) the instrument may be sent for registration under section 860 even if further proceedings are necessary` MEANS
    IF `the charge is created in the United Kingdom but comprises property outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a charge is created in the United Kingdom but comprises property outside the United Kingdom"

§§ `s 867 Charges created in, or over property in, another United Kingdom jurisdiction`

-- src:11913 | (1) Subsection (2) applies where—
-- src:11914 | (a) a charge comprises property situated in a part of the United Kingdom other than the part in which the company is registered, and
-- src:11915 | (b) registration in that other part is necessary to make the charge valid or effectual under the law of that part of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 867(1) Subsection (2) applies where (src:11913-11915)
GIVEN `the charge comprises property situated in a part of the United Kingdom other than the part in which the company is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `registration in that other part is necessary to make the charge valid or effectual under the law of that part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 867(1) subsection (2) applies` MEANS
    IF `the charge comprises property situated in a part of the United Kingdom other than the part in which the company is registered` AND `registration in that other part is necessary to make the charge valid or effectual under the law of that part of the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies where—"

-- src:11916 | (2) The delivery to the registrar of a verified copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced, together with a certificate stating that the charge was presented for registration in that other part of the United Kingdom on the date on which it was so presented has, for the purposes of this Chapter, the same effect as the delivery of the instrument itself.
@ref s 867(2) The delivery to the registrar of a verified copy of the instrument, together with a certificate stating that the charge was presented for registration in that other part, has the same effect as the delivery of the instrument itself (src:11916-11916)
GIVEN `s 867(1) subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a verified copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced is delivered to the registrar together with a certificate stating that the charge was presented for registration in that other part of the United Kingdom on the date on which it was so presented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 867(2) the delivery has the same effect as the delivery of the instrument itself` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 867(1) subsection (2) applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) applies where—"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `a verified copy of the instrument by which the charge is created or evidenced is delivered to the registrar together with a certificate stating that the charge was presented for registration in that other part of the United Kingdom on the date on which it was so presented`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the verified copy and the certificate have not both been delivered

§§ `s 868 Northern Ireland: registration of certain charges etc. affecting land`

-- src:11919 | (1) Where a charge imposed by an order under Article 46 of the 1981 Order or notice of such a charge is registered in the Land Registry against registered land or any estate in registered land of a company, the Registrar of Titles shall as soon as may be cause two copies of the order made under Article 46 of that Order or of any notice under Article 48 of that Order to be delivered to the registrar.
@ref s 868(1) Where a charge imposed by an order under Article 46 of the 1981 Order or notice of such a charge is registered in the Land Registry against registered land, the Registrar of Titles shall as soon as may be cause two copies to be delivered to the registrar (src:11919-11919)
GIVEN `a charge imposed by an order under Article 46 of the 1981 Order, or notice of such a charge, is registered in the Land Registry against registered land or any estate in registered land of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 868(1) the Registrar of Titles must cause two copies to be delivered to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `a charge imposed by an order under Article 46 of the 1981 Order, or notice of such a charge, is registered in the Land Registry against registered land or any estate in registered land of a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a charge imposed by an order under Article 46 of the 1981 Order or notice of such a charge is registered in the Land Registry against registered land or any estate in registered land of a company"

-- src:11920 | (2) Where a charge imposed by an order under Article 46 of the 1981 Order is registered in the Registry of Deeds against any unregistered land or estate in land of a company, the Registrar of Deeds shall as soon as may be cause two copies of the order to be delivered to the registrar.
@ref s 868(2) Where a charge imposed by an order under Article 46 of the 1981 Order is registered in the Registry of Deeds against any unregistered land, the Registrar of Deeds shall as soon as may be cause two copies of the order to be delivered to the registrar (src:11920-11920)
GIVEN `a charge imposed by an order under Article 46 of the 1981 Order is registered in the Registry of Deeds against any unregistered land or estate in land of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 868(2) the Registrar of Deeds must cause two copies of the order to be delivered to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `a charge imposed by an order under Article 46 of the 1981 Order is registered in the Registry of Deeds against any unregistered land or estate in land of a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a charge imposed by an order under Article 46 of the 1981 Order is registered in the Registry of Deeds against any unregistered land or estate in land of a company"

-- src:11921 | (3) On delivery of copies under this section, the registrar shall—
-- src:11922 | (a) register one of them in accordance with section 869, and
@ref s 868(3)(a) On delivery of copies under this section, the registrar shall register one of them in accordance with section 869 (src:11921-11922)
GIVEN `copies have been delivered to the registrar under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 868(3)(a) the registrar must register one of the copies in accordance with section 869` MEANS
    IF `copies have been delivered to the registrar under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On delivery of copies under this section, the registrar shall—"

-- src:11921 | (3) On delivery of copies under this section, the registrar shall—
-- src:11922 | (a) register one of them in accordance with section 869, and
-- src:11923 | (b) not later than 7 days from that date of delivery, cause the other copy together with a certificate of registration under section 869(5) to be sent to the company against which judgment was given.
@ref s 868(3)(b) not later than 7 days from that date of delivery, cause the other copy together with a certificate of registration under section 869(5) to be sent to the company against which judgment was given (src:11921-11923)
GIVEN `the date of delivery of the copies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 868(3)(b) the last day on which the registrar must cause the other copy and the certificate of registration to be sent to the company` MEANS
    `s 859K(2) the last day of 7 days after` `the date of delivery of the copies`

-- src:11924 | (4) Where a charge to which subsection (1) or (2) applies is vacated, the Registrar of Titles or, as the case may be, the Registrar of Deeds shall cause a certified copy of the certificate of satisfaction lodged under Article 132(1) of the 1981 Order to be delivered to the registrar for entry of a memorandum of satisfaction in accordance with section 872.
@ref s 868(4) Where a charge to which subsection (1) or (2) applies is vacated, the Registrar of Titles or the Registrar of Deeds shall cause a certified copy of the certificate of satisfaction to be delivered to the registrar (src:11924-11924)
GIVEN `a charge to which subsection (1) or (2) applies is vacated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 868(4) the Registrar of Titles or the Registrar of Deeds must cause a certified copy of the certificate of satisfaction to be delivered to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `a charge to which subsection (1) or (2) applies is vacated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a charge to which subsection (1) or (2) applies is vacated"

-- s 868(5): the defined expressions, as a table (the meaning is the Act's own words; each refers to another Act or order that is not among the sources)
DECLARE `s 868(5) defined expression` IS ONE OF
    `s 868(5) the 1981 Order`
    `s 868(5) the Registrar of Deeds`
    `s 868(5) Registry of Deeds`
    `s 868(5) Registration of Deeds Acts`
    `s 868(5) the Land Registry`
    `s 868(5) the Registrar of Titles`
    `s 868(5) registered land`
    `s 868(5) unregistered land`

-- src:11925 | (5) In this section—
-- src:11926 | “the 1981 Order” means the Judgments Enforcement (Northern Ireland) Order 1981 (S.I. 1981/226 (N.I. 6));
-- src:11927 | “the Registrar of Deeds” means the registrar appointed under the Registration of Deeds Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 (c. 25);
-- src:11928 | “Registry of Deeds” has the same meaning as in the Registration of Deeds Acts;
-- src:11929 | “Registration of Deeds Acts” means the Registration of Deeds Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 and every statutory provision for the time being in force amending that Act or otherwise relating to the registry of deeds, or the registration of deeds, orders or other instruments or documents in such registry;
-- src:11930 | “the Land Registry” and “the Registrar of Titles” are to be construed in accordance with section 1 of the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 (c. 18);
-- src:11931 | “registered land” and “unregistered land” have the same meaning as in Part 3 of the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970.
@ref s 868(5) In this section the defined expressions (src:11925-11931)
GIVEN expression IS A `s 868(5) defined expression`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 868(5) the meaning the section gives the expression` MEANS
    CONSIDER expression
    WHEN `s 868(5) the 1981 Order` THEN "the Judgments Enforcement (Northern Ireland) Order 1981 (S.I. 1981/226 (N.I. 6))"
    WHEN `s 868(5) the Registrar of Deeds` THEN "the registrar appointed under the Registration of Deeds Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 (c. 25)"
    WHEN `s 868(5) Registry of Deeds` THEN "the same meaning as in the Registration of Deeds Acts"
    WHEN `s 868(5) Registration of Deeds Acts` THEN "the Registration of Deeds Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 and every statutory provision for the time being in force amending that Act"
    WHEN `s 868(5) the Land Registry` THEN "to be construed in accordance with section 1 of the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 (c. 18)"
    WHEN `s 868(5) the Registrar of Titles` THEN "to be construed in accordance with section 1 of the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 (c. 18)"
    WHEN `s 868(5) registered land` THEN "the same meaning as in Part 3 of the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970"
    WHEN `s 868(5) unregistered land` THEN "the same meaning as in Part 3 of the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970"
